\section{The final selected contour}
\label{sec:F}

The selected contour contains an upper anchor moved a fixed distance
inward. This anchor opens both global product gaps and protects the
branch roots. Its parameter disk is therefore larger than the original
radial disk. The proof uses that disk only after bounding the complete
selected integral.
\begin{proposition}\label{prop:F}
The bound \eqref{eq:reqF} holds for the final selected integral.
\end{proposition}
\begin{proof}
We first obtain the protected disk, then estimate the two Pfaffians, and finally differentiate the complete integral. The pointwise group assignments used in the absolute estimates are never differentiated.

