\begin{proposition}[The all-branch complement]\label{prop:allB}
The remaining original all-\(B\) contribution, for
\(N_0+2\le N<D\sqrt H\), is bounded through every \(j\le k\) by
\[
 \exp(C_jN\log(N+1))(H+N)^{C_j}.
\]
\end{proposition}
\begin{proof}
The complement has a named coordinate outside the microcore. We separate configurations far from full equality from those near equality. The former use a two-phase coarea estimate; the latter use the full collision vanishing after all derivatives have been taken.

