This appendix supplies the field-intersection fact used to exclude
smaller even Nickel orders. Its proof also makes explicit the minimal
polynomial input behind the sparse cosine relation.
\begin{lemma}\label{lem:cyclotomic}
If \(p\) is prime and \(p\nmid n\), then
\(\Q(\zeta_p)\cap\Q(\zeta_n)=\Q\).
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
We prove the degree statement by the elementary cyclotomic irreducibility argument and then compare the two field degrees. The coprimality assumption is used in this comparison.

